It is located on the tip of the Punta Banda Peninsula in Baja California, Mexico, approximately 35 kilometers (around 22 miles) southwest of the city of Ensenada. The phenomenon is created when incoming ocean waves push air and water into a partially submerged sea cave, building pressure until water shoots explosively up into the air through an opening in the rocks, frequently reaching heights of up to 30 meters (nearly 100 feet).

